#: data/missions/01_bell_of_grebastica/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Bell of Grebaštica"
msgstr "Колокол Гребаштицы"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/01_bell_of_grebastica/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Aga's men took the bell of Grebaštica as a \"tax\". Follow its trail along the coast and bring"
" it home."
msgstr ""
"Люди Аги забрали колокол Гребаштицы как «налог». {crew|Пройди|Пройди|Пройдите} по его следу вдоль "
"берега и {crew|верни|верни|верните} его домой."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/01_bell_of_grebastica/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The cathedral of St. James in Šibenik was built only of stone, without wood or bricks. Its outer "
"wall carries 71 carved heads of the people of that time."
msgstr ""
"Собор Святого Иакова в Шибенике построен только из камня, без дерева и кирпича. На его внешней "
"стене — 71 каменная голова: лица людей того времени."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/01_bell_of_grebastica/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The bell rings again!"
msgstr "Колокол снова звонит!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/01_bell_of_grebastica/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The bell of Grebaštica is home, and it rings over the whole bay."
msgstr "Колокол Гребаштицы снова дома и звонит над всей бухтой."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/01_bell_of_grebastica/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The children wave from the stone walls."
msgstr "Дети машут с каменных стен."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/02_shipwright_of_korcula/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, please help me! I am Katarina, the daughter of Master Ivan."
