"Хм... разве что {crew|ты отгадаешь|ты отгадаешь|вы отгадаете} мои загадки. Граф любит загадки."

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ha! Wrong! Think again, captain."
msgstr "Ха! Неверно! {crew|Подумай|Подумай|Подумайте} ещё, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}."

#. what a judge says after the right answers, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Grr! You know too much."
msgstr "Ррр! Слишком много {crew|ты знаешь|ты знаешь|вы знаете}."

#. what a judge says after the right answers, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Go then, all of you... toll-free!"
msgstr "Ну идите, все... без пошлины!"

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the pilgrims to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} паломников {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Welcome to Loreto, pilgrims!"
msgstr "Добро пожаловать в Лорето, паломники!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "And not a single coin for the Count's toll."
msgstr "И ни одной монетки на пошлину графу."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The pilgrims pray in the Holy House, and they sing all the way home."
msgstr "Паломники молятся в Святом доме и поют всю дорогу домой."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "And the Count's toll man? He went home to think about riddles."
msgstr "А сборщик пошлин графа? Ушёл домой думать над загадками."

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Pilgrims of Loreto"
msgstr "Паломники Лорето"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Carry the pilgrims of Pescara past the Count's \"pilgrim toll\" to the Holy House of Loreto."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Провези|Провези|Провезите} паломников из Пескары мимо «пошлины для паломников» графа к "
"Святому дому в Лорето."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A legend says that angels carried the Holy House of Mary from Nazareth to Loreto. Because of that "
"flying house, the Madonna of Loreto became the patron saint of pilots in 1920."
msgstr ""
"По легенде, ангелы перенесли Святой дом Марии из Назарета в Лорето. Из-за этого летающего дома "
"Мадонна Лоретская в 1920 году стала покровительницей лётчиков."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The pilgrims reached Loreto!"
msgstr "Паломники в Лорето!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You carried the pilgrims past the Count's toll."
msgstr "{crew|Ты провёз|Ты провезла|Вы провезли} паломников мимо пошлины графа."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Not one of them paid a coin."
msgstr "Никто из них не заплатил ни монетки."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Count's toll man left behind a page of the Count's charter."
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, сборщик пошлин графа оставил страницу из грамоты графа."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count says it is twenty years old. A paper merchant could tell!"
msgstr "Граф говорит, ей двадцать лет. Торговец бумагой сразу понял бы!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ser Anselmo of Fabriano sails along the coast. Find him!"
msgstr "Сер Ансельмо из Фабриано плавает вдоль берега. {crew|Найди|Найди|Найдите} его!"

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The paper merchant has {hallmark}."
msgstr "У торговца бумагой {hallmark}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen Ser Anselmo, the paper merchant?"
msgstr "Вы видели сера Ансельмо, торговца бумагой?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He is here, at the market! But which one is he?"
msgstr "Он здесь, на рынке! Но кто же из них он?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is Ser Anselmo? Remember what the people told you!"
msgstr "Кто из них сер Ансельмо? {crew|Вспомни|Вспомни|Вспомните}, что говорили люди!"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not Ser Anselmo! Think of everything you heard."
msgstr ""
"Нет, это не сер Ансельмо! {crew|Вспомни|Вспомни|Вспомните} всё, что {crew|ты слышал|ты слышала|вы "
"слышали}."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"A paper with a secret? Take me to it, captain!\""
msgstr "«Бумага с секретом? {crew|Вези|Вези|Везите} меня к ней, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}!»"

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring Ser Anselmo to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} сера Ансельмо {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ser Anselmo holds the page against the light."
msgstr "Сер Ансельмо смотрит страницу на свет."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"See the watermark? This paper was made in Fabriano only this year!\""
msgstr "«Видите водяной знак? Эту бумагу сделали в Фабриано только в этом году!»"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "So it can not be twenty years old. That is our first proof!"
msgstr "Значит, ей не может быть двадцать лет. Это наше первое доказательство!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A watermark never lies, captain."
msgstr "Водяной знак никогда не лжёт, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count can forge words, but not the paper of Fabriano!"
msgstr "Граф умеет подделать слова, но не бумагу из Фабриано!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Paper with a Secret"
msgstr "Бумага с секретом"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Find the paper merchant who can read the charter against the light. Proof 1: the watermark of "
"Fabriano."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Найди|Найди|Найдите} торговца бумагой, который посмотрит грамоту на просвет. Доказательство "
"1: водяной знак Фабриано."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The paper mills of Fabriano were among the first in Europe. Their papermakers invented the "
"watermark: a picture inside the paper, which shows only against the light."
msgstr ""
"Бумажные мельницы Фабриано были одними из первых в Европе. Их мастера придумали водяной знак: "
"рисунок внутри бумаги, который виден только на свет."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The first proof!"
msgstr "Первое доказательство!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You found Ser Anselmo, and the watermark speaks."
msgstr "{crew|Ты нашёл|Ты нашла|Вы нашли} сера Ансельмо, и водяной знак заговорил."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count's paper is new, not twenty years old."
msgstr "Бумага графа новая, ей не двадцать лет."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Count's seal looks like the seal of the Viceroy."
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, печать графа похожа на печать вице-короля."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A seal-maker of Ortona carved seals for him, then quit and hid."
msgstr "Резчик печатей из Ортоны делал для него печати, а потом ушёл и спрятался."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Find him! He can tell the judges the truth."
msgstr "{crew|Найди|Найди|Найдите} его! Он может рассказать судьям правду."

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The seal-maker has {hallmark}."
msgstr "У резчика печатей {hallmark}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen the seal-maker who hides from the Count?"
msgstr "Вы видели резчика печатей, который прячется от графа?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He is hiding here, among the craftsmen! But which one is he?"
msgstr "Он прячется здесь, среди ремесленников! Но кто же из них он?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is the seal-maker? Remember what the people told you!"
msgstr "Кто из них резчик печатей? {crew|Вспомни|Вспомни|Вспомните}, что говорили люди!"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not the seal-maker! Think of everything you heard."
msgstr ""
"Нет, это не резчик печатей! {crew|Вспомни|Вспомни|Вспомните} всё, что {crew|ты слышал|ты "
"слышала|вы слышали}."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"Yes, I carved the Count's seal. He said it was for a play!\" Mastro Nunzio gives you the mould."
msgstr ""
"«Да, я вырезал печать графа. Он сказал, что она для спектакля!» Мастро Нунцио отдаёт форму печати."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the mould of the seal to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} форму печати {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Look: the name of the King is spelt wrong on it!"
msgstr "Смотрите: имя короля на ней написано с ошибкой!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No seal of the Viceroy has such a mistake. That is our second proof!"
msgstr "Ни на одной печати вице-короля нет такой ошибки. Это наше второе доказательство!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will tell the judges everything, captain."
msgstr "Я всё расскажу судьям, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "From now on, I carve only honest seals!"
msgstr "Теперь я вырезаю только честные печати!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Seal-Maker of Ortona"
msgstr "Резчик печатей из Ортоны"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Find the seal-maker who quit the Count and hid. Proof 2: the false seal."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Найди|Найди|Найдите} резчика печатей, который ушёл от графа и спрятался. Доказательство 2: "
"фальшивая печать."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Ortona keeps the bones of St. Thomas the Apostle. Sailors of Ortona brought them from the Greek "
"island of Chios in 1258."
msgstr ""
"В Ортоне хранятся мощи апостола Фомы. Моряки из Ортоны привезли их с греческого острова Хиос в "
"1258 году."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The second proof!"
msgstr "Второе доказательство!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You found Mastro Nunzio, and the false seal is in Trani."
msgstr "{crew|Ты нашёл|Ты нашла|Вы нашли} мастро Нунцио, и фальшивая печать теперь в Трани."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count spelt the name of the King wrong!"
msgstr "Граф написал имя короля с ошибкой!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, an old fisherman here remembers the Count from long ago."
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, один старый рыбак здесь помнит графа с давних времён."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He says the Count was no count at all, but a young copyist: Bepi Sgorbio!"
msgstr "Он говорит, что граф вовсе не граф, а молодой переписчик: Бепи Сгорбио!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bepi lived on the Gargano. Ask about him there."
msgstr "Бепи жил на Гаргано. {crew|Спроси|Спроси|Спросите} о нём там."

#. a clue; {fact} is a noun phrase like 'the town with the great Roman arena'
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bepi had a friend in {fact}."
msgstr "Говорят, друг Бепи переехал {fact@to}."

#. a clue; {fact} is a noun phrase like 'the town with the great Roman arena'
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ask in {fact}. They knew Bepi there."
msgstr "{crew|Сплавай|Сплавай|Сплавайте} {fact@to}: там знали Бепи."

#. a clue; {fact} is a noun phrase like 'the town with the great Roman arena'
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bepi copied letters for the people of {fact}."
msgstr "Бепи часто рассказывал {fact@about}: он переписывал там письма."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Did you know Bepi Sgorbio, the copyist?"
msgstr "Вы знали Бепи Сгорбио, переписчика?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bepi? He hid a box of his old letters in the cave under the white rock of Vieste!"
msgstr "Бепи? Он спрятал ящик со старыми письмами в пещере под белой скалой Вьесте!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cave under the white rock? I know the way, even in a storm!"
msgstr "Пещера под белой скалой? Я знаю дорогу, даже в шторм!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is the box. The letters are signed: Bepi Sgorbio, copyist."
msgstr "Вот ящик. Письма подписаны: Бепи Сгорбио, переписчик."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fetch Bepi's old letters from the white rock."
msgstr "{crew|Забери|Забери|Заберите} старые письма Бепи у белой скалы."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring Bepi's letters to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} письма Бепи {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Let me compare them with the Count's charter..."
msgstr "Дайте сравнить их с грамотой графа..."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The same hand wrote them both! That is our third proof!"
msgstr "Их писала одна и та же рука! Это наше третье доказательство!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Three proofs, captain: the paper, the seal and the letters!"
msgstr "Три доказательства, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}: бумага, печать и письма!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The \"Count\" is nobody but Bepi Sgorbio."
msgstr "«Граф» — это всего лишь Бепи Сгорбио."

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The White Rock"
msgstr "Белая скала"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Storms around the Gargano. Under the white rock of Pizzomunno lie Bepi's old letters. Proof 3."
msgstr "Штормы у Гаргано. Под белой скалой Пиццомунно лежат старые письма Бепи. Доказательство 3."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The tall white rock on the beach of Vieste is called Pizzomunno. A legend says it is a young "
"fisherman who turned to stone while he waited for his love Cristalda, whom the mermaids took away."
msgstr ""
"Высокая белая скала на пляже Вьесте зовётся Пиццомунно. По легенде, это молодой рыбак: он "
"окаменел, пока ждал свою любимую Кристальду, которую унесли русалки."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The third proof!"
msgstr "Третье доказательство!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You braved the storms of the Gargano."
msgstr "{crew|Ты не испугался|Ты не испугалась|Вы не испугались} штормов Гаргано."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bepi's old letters show who the Count really is."
msgstr "Старые письма Бепи показывают, кто такой граф на самом деле."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Count is furious about the three proofs."
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, граф в ярости из-за трёх доказательств."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He dares you to a regatta at Barletta: thirteen boats, like the thirteen knights of 1503!"
msgstr ""
"Он вызывает {crew|тебя|тебя|вас} на регату в Барлетте: тринадцать лодок, как тринадцать рыцарей "
"1503 года!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "If you win, the whole coast will see that his charms are nothing."
msgstr ""
"Если {crew|ты победишь|ты победишь|вы победите}, весь берег увидит, что его амулеты — пустышка."

#. what a rival says when he dares the crew to a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Welcome to the Challenge of Barletta, captain!"
msgstr "Добро пожаловать на Вызов Барлетты, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}!"

#. what a rival says when he dares the crew to a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Thirteen boats, three buoys, and glory for the winner!"
msgstr "Тринадцать лодок, три буя и слава победителю!"

#. what a rival says when he dares the crew to a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "My yellow boat will leave you all behind!"
msgstr "Моя жёлтая лодка оставит вас всех позади!"

#. what a rival says before a rematch of a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ha! Back for another lesson?"
msgstr "Ха! {crew|Вернулся|Вернулась|Вернулись} за новым уроком?"

#. what a rival says before a rematch of a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Again: thirteen boats, three buoys!"
msgstr "Снова: тринадцать лодок, три буя!"

#. what the crew hears after winning a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Impossible! I took the short way, and you still won?"
msgstr "Не может быть! Я срезал путь, а {crew|ты|ты|вы} всё равно {crew|победил|победила|победили}?"

#. what the crew hears after winning a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The crowd of Barletta cheers for the fair captain!"
msgstr "Толпа Барлетты ликует: слава {crew|честному капитану|честному капитану|честным капитанам}!"

#. what the crew hears when a rival won the race, one short sentence
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count was back first, but he cheated! The fishermen ask for a rematch tomorrow."
msgstr "Граф вернулся первым, но он сжульничал! Рыбаки просят завтра реванш."

#. what the crew hears when a rival cheats in a race, one short sentence
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count cuts through the shallows and skips a buoy! That's cheating!"
msgstr "Граф срезает путь через мели и пропускает буй! Это жульничество!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The whole town saw it: the Count cheated, and you won fairly!"
msgstr "Весь город видел: граф жульничал, а {crew|ты победил|ты победила|вы победили} честно!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I hammered you a horseshoe, for luck."
msgstr "Я выковал {crew|тебе|тебе|вам} подкову на счастье."

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Challenge of Barletta"
msgstr "Вызов Барлетты"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Count dares the crew to a regatta of thirteen boats, as the thirteen knights of 1503. He "
"cheats through the shallows; the crew wins fairly."
msgstr ""
"Граф вызывает команду на регату тринадцати лодок, как тринадцать рыцарей 1503 года. Он срезает "
"путь через мели, но команда побеждает честно."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Challenge of Barletta in 1503 began with an insult at a dinner: a French knight said that the "
"Italians were poor knights. Thirteen knights of each side met in a tournament, and the Italians "
"won."
msgstr ""
"Вызов Барлетты в 1503 году начался с обиды за ужином: французский рыцарь сказал, что итальянцы — "
"плохие рыцари. По тринадцать рыцарей с каждой стороны сошлись на турнире, и итальянцы победили."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A fair win!"
msgstr "Честная победа!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count cut through the shallows, and still you won."
msgstr "Граф срезал путь через мели, а {crew|ты|ты|вы} всё равно {crew|победил|победила|победили}."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "All of Barletta saw who sails fairly."
msgstr "Вся Барлетта видела, кто ходит под парусом честно."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain! It's me, Luka, the ship's boy. Remember?"
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}! Это я, юнга Лука. {crew|Помнишь|Помнишь|Помните}?"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count bought up all the olive oil, and he sells it at three times the price."
msgstr "Граф скупил всё оливковое масло и продаёт его втрое дороже."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But Vito of Monopoli hid some olives. Help him press them!"
msgstr "Но Вито из Монополи спрятал немного оливок. {crew|Помоги|Помоги|Помогите} ему их отжать!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take this salt along: on this coast, salt buys almost anything."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Возьми|Возьми|Возьмите} с собой эту соль: на этом берегу за соль можно купить почти всё."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "My olives are picked, but the Count's men took my pressing mats."
msgstr "Мои оливки собраны, но люди графа забрали мои циновки для пресса."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Without mats, the press gives no oil. Donata of Brindisi weaves them!"
msgstr "Без циновок пресс не даёт масла. Их плетёт Доната из Бриндизи!"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fine mats! The press is turning..."
msgstr "Отличные циновки! Пресс крутится..."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is the oil, captain. Take it to the market of Bari."
msgstr ""
"Вот масло, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}. {crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} его на рынок в Бари."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I weave pressing mats from rushes."
msgstr "Я плету циновки для пресса из камыша."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But I need salt for my fish. Do you have salt?"
msgstr "Но мне нужна соль для рыбы. У {crew|тебя|тебя|вас} есть соль?"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Salt! Now my fish keeps all winter."
msgstr "Соль! Теперь моя рыба пролежит всю зиму."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here are my best pressing mats."
msgstr "Вот мои лучшие циновки для пресса."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the oil to the market of {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} масло на рынок, {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Oil from Monopoli, at a fair price!"
msgstr "Масло из Монополи, по честной цене!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now everybody in Bari can cook again."
msgstr "Теперь все в Бари снова могут готовить."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count's oil sits in his cellar, and nobody buys it!"
msgstr "Масло графа стоит у него в погребе, и никто его не покупает!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, I will keep my eyes open for him."
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, я буду за ним приглядывать."

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Oil for Monopoli"
msgstr "Масло для Монополи"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Count hoards the olive oil. Trade salt for pressing mats, the mats for oil, and bring it to "
"the market of Bari."
msgstr ""
"Граф прячет оливковое масло. {crew|Обменяй|Обменяй|Обменяйте} соль на циновки, циновки на масло и "
"{crew|отвези|отвези|отвезите} его на рынок Бари."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In Apulia, many olive mills were dug into the rock under the ground. It was warm down there in "
"winter, so the oil flowed better."
msgstr ""
"В Апулии многие маслодельни вырубали в скале под землёй. Зимой там было тепло, и масло текло "
"лучше."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fair oil for Bari!"
msgstr "Честное масло для Бари!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Salt, mats and a lot of sailing beat the Count's prices."
msgstr "Соль, циновки и долгое плавание победили цены графа."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The kitchens of Bari smell of fresh oil."
msgstr "На кухнях Бари пахнет свежим маслом."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Count has fled with his Golden Charter!"
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, граф сбежал со своей Золотой грамотой!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Without the charter, the judges can not see his forgery."
msgstr "Без грамоты судьи не увидят его подделку."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Chase him! A man so fine can not hide for long."
msgstr "{crew|Догони|Догони|Догоните} его! Такой нарядный господин долго не спрячется."

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count had {hallmark}."
msgstr "Графа легко узнать: у него {hallmark}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen Count Malvento?"
msgstr "Вы видели графа Мальвенто?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is the Count?"
msgstr "Кто из них граф?"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not the Count! Remember all four things you learned."
msgstr "Нет, это не граф! {crew|Вспомни|Вспомни|Вспомните} все четыре приметы."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"Alright, alright! Here is the charter. It was such a beautiful charter...\""
msgstr "«Ладно, ладно! Вот грамота. Такая была красивая грамота...»"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"Fine, I will come before the judges in Trani.\""
msgstr "«Хорошо, я предстану перед судьями в Трани»."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "With the Golden Charter, the crew holds everything the judges need."
msgstr "С Золотой грамотой у команды есть всё, что нужно судьям."

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count Flees"
msgstr "Граф бежит"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Count flees with his charter. Yellow gloves, a smell of violets, a wig too big, a ring with a "
"false seal."
msgstr ""
"Граф бежит со своей грамотой. Жёлтые перчатки, запах фиалок, слишком большой парик, перстень с "
"фальшивой печатью."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Around 1600, perfumed gloves were the height of fashion. Gloves were scented with violets, roses "
"or amber, also to hide the smell of the leather."
msgstr ""
"Около 1600 года надушенные перчатки были в большой моде. Их душили фиалками, розами или амброй, в "
"том числе чтобы скрыть запах кожи."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The charter is yours!"
msgstr "Грамота у {crew|тебя|тебя|вас}!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You chased the Count along the whole coast and found him."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Ты гнался|Ты гналась|Вы гнались} за графом вдоль всего берега и {crew|нашёл|нашла|нашли} "
"его."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the crew holds the Golden Charter."
msgstr "Теперь Золотая грамота у команды."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the judges of the Royal Audience in Trani are ready."
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, судьи Королевской аудиенции в Трани готовы."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring them the proofs and the witnesses:"
msgstr "{crew|Привези|Привези|Привезите} им доказательства и свидетелей:"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Luka here in Bari, Michele in Manfredonia and Vito in Monopoli."
msgstr "Луку здесь, в Бари, Микеле в Манфредонии и Вито в Монополи."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I am ready, captain! I saw the Count take the tolls in Bari."
msgstr "Я готов, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}! Я видел, как граф брал пошлины в Бари."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I knew Bepi when he was a young copyist."
msgstr "Я знал Бепи, когда он был молодым переписчиком."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will tell the judges, captain."
msgstr "Я всё расскажу судьям, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will tell the judges how the Count hoarded the oil."
msgstr "Я расскажу судьям, как граф прятал масло."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the proofs and the witnesses to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Доставь|Доставь|Доставьте} доказательства и свидетелей {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "So this is the Golden Charter. Show me your proofs, captain."
msgstr ""
"Так вот она, Золотая грамота. {crew|Покажи|Покажи|Покажите} доказательства, "
"{crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The watermark of Fabriano: this paper is new, not twenty years old."
msgstr "Водяной знак Фабриано: эта бумага новая, ей не двадцать лет."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A seal with the name of the King spelt wrong!"
msgstr "Печать, на которой имя короля написано с ошибкой!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "And the same hand wrote these letters and the charter."
msgstr "И эти письма и грамоту писала одна и та же рука."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
